  "starterCode": "import pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_boolean_indexing(records: list, filter_col: str, threshold: float) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Boolean Indexing** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_boolean_indexing(records: list, filter_col: str, threshold: float) -> list:\n    df = pd.DataFrame(records)\n    return df[df[filter_col] > float(threshold)].to_dict(orient='records')\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
